# SemText npl-poa — plan-of-action block, all display states
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house convention). Three example panels in one
# frame, one per display state the tag provides: the enhanced render of the
# default `direction="lr"` block, the enhanced `direction="td"` variant, and
# the JS-off degrade (no bundle). The invariants the design must broadcast:
# the decision tree is ALWAYS readable mermaid source in a code block (the
# component never renders a diagram — no mermaid runtime, ever), the chosen
# path is featured ONCE prominently as a generated "selected" block, and the
# authored `<selected>` line stays visible beneath it (quieter, never hidden).
#
# MODE 1 — enhanced, direction="lr" (default):
#   visible: a bordered dark code block holding three lines of mermaid
#     source (graph LR + two weighted edges), below it two short prose lines
#     — one per weighted path — then one dim small line (the authored
#     selected path), and the panel's most prominent element: a full-width
#     "selected" block with a 3px violet accent bar on its left edge, a
#     faint violet tint fill, a small-caps violet "selected" label followed
#     by a middot and the chosen path in brighter text.
#   must never: render the fence as an actual diagram, chart, boxes-and-
#     arrows figure, or anything but monospace source; fuse the small-caps
#     label into the sentence (the middot separator is mandatory); hide,
#     blur, or remove the authored selected line; fill the choice block
#     opaque.
# MODE 2 — enhanced, direction="td":
#   visible: the identical anatomy — code block (graph TD source), reasoning
#     prose lines, quiet authored line, prominent selected block. The ONLY
#     difference from mode 1 is the fence's first source line (top-down
#     spelling); no visual direction arrow, no rotated layout.
#   must never: restyle any element differently from mode 1 or add a visual
#     flow diagram to "express" the direction.
# MODE 3 — JS-off degrade (no bundle):
#   visible: the same fence code block, the weighted-path prose lines, and
#     the selected path as one plain prose line — NO accent bar, NO tint, NO
#     small-caps label, NO generated block of any kind.
#   must never: keep any enhanced chrome in this panel (that would break the
#     nothing-hidden-nothing-generated JS-off contract); collapse the prose
#     into a run-on paragraph (weighted paths read one per line).
#
# Reference snapshots are harness output in
# .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-poa/ (npm run snap:tag -- npl-poa;
# per-figure source shots failed capture this run — see
# reports/tag-npl-poa.md — so the fullpage PNGs are attached; they show the
# reference page, attribute table and authored source context).
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-poa
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of three side-by-side reference-page panels
    illustrating one plan-of-action block in its three display states, wide
    16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D). Dark slate
    navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and a faint
    violet radial glow upper-left. Three equal panels sit side by side,
    separated by thin slate hairline dividers, each panel a dark slate card
    (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, squared corners, deep soft
    shadow; a small dim caption bar sits above each panel.

    Every panel stacks the SAME three-row anatomy top to bottom. Row 1: a
    dark bordered code block (hairline slate border, squared 8px corners,
    slightly darker fill than the card) holding three short lines of
    placeholder monospace source bars — a lead line then two indented
    branch lines, each branch line ending in a small violet weight chip
    (a tiny rounded bar suggesting "90%" / "40%" weights). Row 2: two short
    near-white prose lines, one per branch, each carrying a small violet
    weight chip — the weighted reasoning, one path per line, never a fused
    paragraph. Row 3 differs by panel.

    Left panel — ENHANCED, default direction. Row 3a: one very short dim
    muted slate prose line (the authored record of the choice). Row 3b, the
    most prominent element in the panel: a full-width block with a 3px
    violet (#7C3AED) accent bar on its left edge, a barely-there violet tint
    fill (#7C3AED at 12% over the card), squared 6px corners; inside it a
    small-caps violet label bar (short), then a middot separator, then one
    bright near-white placeholder bar (the chosen path) — label clearly
    separated, never fused with the path.

    Middle panel — ENHANCED, top-down variant. Identical to the left panel
    in every measure (accent bar, tint, label, brightness, spacing); only
    the code block's lead source line differs (same placeholder-bar look).
    Nothing else changes.

    Right panel — JS-OFF DEGRADE. Rows 1 and 2 identical; row 3 is a single
    plain dim prose line aligned with the reasoning lines — no accent bar,
    no tint, no small-caps label, no generated block. The panel must read
    as the same document with the enhancement layer switched off.

    The three panels must be pixel-comparable in rows 1-2; only row 3
    differentiates them. All copy stays abstract placeholder bars —
    strictly no letters, digits, or words anywhere; weight chips are
    abstract violet ticks, not numerals.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, 3D, photorealism,
    faces, avatars, robot mascots, more than three panels, a rendered flow
    diagram, boxes-and-arrows chart, graph nodes with real edges, opaque
    filled selected block, the selected label fused with the path text,
    enhanced chrome (accent bar, tint, label) in the right JS-off panel, a
    missing or blurred authored selected line
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, three-panel state comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-poa/npl-poa-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: reference page at 1280 — chrome, attribute table, authored
      source of the primary example (source-only view)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-poa/npl-poa-fullpage-390.png
    role: reference
    description: reference page at 390 — mobile context of the same page

requirements:
  subject: three panels of one plan-of-action block — left enhanced default
    with quiet authored line + prominent selected block, middle enhanced
    top-down variant identical except the fence source, right JS-off
    degrade with plain prose only
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet
    accent bar and tint on the selected block only, near-white prose bars,
    muted slate authored line, violet weight chips
  composition: three equal panels side by side, the three-row anatomy at a
    consistent vertical rhythm, rows 1-2 pixel-comparable across panels
  do:
    - keep the code block unmistakably monospace source, never a diagram
    - keep the selected block the single most prominent element in the two
      enhanced panels
    - keep the authored selected line visible (dimmer) beneath the selected
      block in the enhanced panels
    - render weighted reasoning as one line per path, never fused
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, real logos, or a rendered mermaid diagram
    - enhanced chrome of any kind in the JS-off panel
    - hiding, blurring, or deleting the authored selected line
    - a small-caps label fused with the chosen-path text

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - state_differentiation
    - source_not_diagram
    - choice_prominence
  criteria:
    state_differentiation:
      weight: 3
      description: Left has quiet line + selected block; middle is identical
        except the fence source line; right has plain prose only — no
        enhanced chrome
      fail_signals:
        - accent bar, tint, or label present in the right panel
        - selected block missing from the left or middle panel
        - panel anatomy differs beyond the row-3 difference
    source_not_diagram:
      weight: 3
      description: Row 1 reads as monospace source in a bordered code block
        in all three panels
      fail_signals:
        - any drawn diagram, nodes, edges, or chart shape
        - a missing or restyled code block in any panel
    choice_prominence:
      weight: 3
      description: The selected block is the most prominent element in the
        enhanced panels; label and path are separated by a middot; the
        authored line stays visible beneath
      fail_signals:
        - the authored selected line hidden, blurred, or absent
        - label fused with the path text
        - the selected block dimmer than the reasoning rows
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style
      fail_signals:
        - light theme
        - glossy 3D look
        - rounded card corners
  reject_if:
    - any legible text, letters, digits, watermark, or logo
    - a rendered diagram in place of the mermaid source anywhere
    - enhanced chrome in the JS-off panel
    - more than three panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-poa
